        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}$",
          "worked": "The radius is $2x$. The radius bisecting the chord is perpendicular to it.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+4^2&=(2x)^2\\\\3x^2&=16\\\\x^2&=\\frac{16}{3}\\\\x&=\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
